      "raw_response": " D. Canada is a part of the UK for historical reasons (specifically, due to British colonization).\n\nHistorically, Canada was a British colony and later a dominion of the British Empire. The British Crown acquired much of Canada during the 18th and 19th centuries through a series of treaties and wars, primarily with the French, the indigenous peoples, and the United States. Canada became a self-governing dominion in 1867, but it remained part of the British Empire until it formally severed its last constitutional ties with the UK in 1982 through the passage of the Canada Act.\n\nToday, Canada is an independent sovereign state, with its own government, military, and currency. While it remains part of the British Commonwealth, it is not a part of the United Kingdom.\n\nANSWER: D",
